meteotemplate - weewx extension that sends data to a meteotemplate instance
Copyright 2016-2020 Matthew Wall
Distributed under terms of the GPLv3

This extension uploads data to meteotemplate version 12 or later.

===============================================================================
Installation

1) download the extension

wget -O weewx-meteotemplate.zip https://github.com/weewx-packages/weewx-meteotemplate/archive/master.zip

2) run the installer:

wee_extension --install weewx-meteotemplate.zip

3) enter parameters in weewx.conf:

[StdRESTful]
    [[Meteotemplate]]
        server_url = INSERT_SERVER_URL_HERE
        password = INSERT_PASSWORD_HERE

4) restart weewx:

sudo /etc/init.d/weewx stop
sudo /etc/init.d/weewx start


===============================================================================
Options

The server_url is the full path to the meteotemplate api script.  It should
be something like this:

  https://localhost/template/api.php

The password is the upload password, not the password used to administrate
the meteotemplate installation.

The default configuration will send data every archive interval.  To send
data on each LOOP packet, change the binding:

    [[Meteotemplate]]
        binding = loop

Additional sensors

Map API parameter names to WeeWX observations under field_map:

[StdRESTful]
    [[Meteotemplate]]
        [[[field_map]]]
            PP1 = pm2_5
            PP2 = pm10
            L = lightning_strike_count

Only measurements present in the packet are sent. A WH41 provides PM2.5;
this extension cannot derive a PM10 measurement from PM2.5. Confirm the
parameter names supported by your installed api.php version.

R is the daily cumulative rain, filled from the archive when dayRain is
absent. A reachable archive with rain records is needed for that sum. The
update password is the Meteotemplate update password, not its admin login.
Non-Success API replies remain upload failures and appear in the WeeWX log.

